  "summary": "One working day on a five-person team, from the first branch to the last rescue: start a feature, collide with a teammate, rebase and squash for review, backport a hotfix with cherry-pick, and recover a lost commit with the reflog. Each stage mixes predict-the-output drills with real Git in your own clone, against a bare origin that teammates push to.",
